{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR-2, cheap checks first. Head a724b01ca262dcb20b5f47c6c3b4d7a389c216bf, tree 4e9f84b6b9e347d0fd24b965b5390194c3f05f27, branch builder/br2-cheap-checks-20261025: six commits on Main 2f5d9a2f, 19 paths, all 19 named by the artifacts. Review request 99106a15, checker promise bc2344b6, request 777e234d.\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request 777e234d and finding TD-05 in the review note; the diff of package.json, scripts/gate.sh, scripts/test.mjs, scripts/test-summary.mjs, scripts/test-progress.mjs, the four vitest configs, the Counting scripts, the replay test and docs/testing.md; the owning test scripts/test.test.mjs; the stop-guard control commit 894f10a7; then the gate 3310 records.\n\nBase. The head sits on 2f5d9a2f, not on Main 5248b0be. The only change between those two commits is examples/grow/runbook.md, which this head does not touch, and git merge-tree merges the head onto 5248b0be with no conflict.\n\nHead and gate. The head differs from the gated checkpoint 0b245ed4 (tree d225abb2) only in the primary note. Source, tests, config and dependencies are those of the gated checkpoint, so the documents-only follow-up rule applies and no second gate is owed. The failed gate 82795 and the failed Node 22 baseline 44405 stay recorded as failures. The note does not use the isolated follow-up 16214 to validate the later reporter change; the fresh gate 3310 does that.\n\nAcceptance, both parts met:\n1. \"A failure in a plain project or a post-runner check stops the gate before the Worker test project starts.\" scripts/test.mjs runs five fixed stages: kernel, node, counting, plain, native. It stops at the first stage that fails, is signalled or cannot spawn, and records the later stages as unreached. The Node files and the Counting check, which used to run after the whole Vitest run, now run first. The plain view selects its fourteen projects before Vitest resolves the inherited package configs, so no workerd project starts in that view. The owning test covers a plain failure, a spawn failure and a signal, and checks that a native sentinel file is never written. Control 894f10a7 changes only the stop guard to false. In its records, the plain-failure case fails at test.test.mjs:45 and the spawn case at :56, so the test can detect a broken guard. I read the records; I did not rerun the control.\n2. \"Each gate ends with its ten slowest cases and time per project.\" The EXIT trap in gate.sh always runs test-summary.mjs, including after a failure before the test step. In gate 3310's stdout, the summary lists ten cases with known durations and a duration sum for each of the sixteen Vitest projects, then the Node and Counting case sums.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The old single run already ran its groups in order: group 0 (the plain projects), then scope, then scope-denial. Splitting it into a plain run and a native run therefore puts nothing in series that ran in parallel before; the cost is one more Vitest start. The sixteen project declarations are kept once, in vitest.projects.mjs, with a check that the partition is exactly fourteen plain and two native projects. vitest.config.ts still loads all sixteen projects for focused commands and for test-changed.mjs. In gate 3310, kernel, node and counting together took 37.4 s and plain took 59.1 s, before 1,255.5 s of native. A failure in a cheap stage or a plain project now stops before about 21 minutes of native work; that is the saving TD-05 asked for. A failed stage keeps its own exit code, and a summary failure turns only an otherwise passing run into a failure. The replay test repair is in scope: the gate needed it to pass. It replaces one git hash-object process per object with the SHA-1 loose writer on a SHA-1 bare repository, followed by one cat-file --batch-check. Each returned ID is checked against the built object, and fsck, replay, every original assertion and the 30 s deadline are kept.\n\nSecurity: no new authority. This is local test tooling. Evidence files are opened with wx and mode 0600, and the evidence directory is mkdtemp or a new directory with mode 0700. Each child gets only its own stage's observation variables. The Counting observation takes only an absolute destination and a local file: URL for the reporter, and it refuses incomplete settings before the build. The reporter records public test event fields and no logs, error text or stdout. No production code, Worker, seal or deploy file changes, and no deployment is needed.\n\nSimplification: acceptable, with three nonblocking notes.\n- The head adds about 1,050 lines for a request sized small. test-summary.mjs (158 dense lines) does identity reconciliation, Node 22 compatibility and Counting source mapping, which is more than the acceptance needs. Because issues fail a passing run, the summary is also a new way for a healthy gate to fail. If a reporting-only failure shows up in a later gate, treat it as TD-07 work and consider making those issues warnings.\n- Each stage row carries userMs and systemMs, which are always null, so every gate prints \"user unknown; system unknown\" five times. Measure them or drop the fields. Also, vitest.projects.mjs keeps the six-space indentation it had inside the old config.\n- scripts/test-changed.mjs runs every test when a root file such as vitest.config.ts changes, but its pattern does not include the new vitest.projects.mjs, vitest.plain.config.ts or vitest.native.config.ts. A later edit to the project list would then run only the tests --changed selects. Add the three names in a later head.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- The digests of evidence-index.json (64ae828d…) and the packet manifest (74fbca37…) match assert 7efbae9d. The gate 3310 manifest (ac6bb9bb…) and result.json (85b4d0e4…) match the index, and all 39 files in that manifest match their SHA-256 digests.\n- In result.json, exitCode is 0, with expectedHead 0b245ed4 and expectedTree d225abb2. In gate.stdout.log, the head line shows changed files 0, install is skipped against the lockfile, and every step exits 0. Node shows 53 passed and Counting 55. Plain shows 2,816 passed and 1 skipped (2,817), and native 769 passed and 2 skipped (771). The summary reports 57 unknown observations and 0 contradictory records, and stderr is empty.\n- git diff --check is clean over the branch. All six commit subjects are 63 characters or fewer.\n- The timing, load and Node 22/26 figures in the note are the builder's observations; I did not rerun them.\n\nNote for the planner: BR-4 lists \"archive-git-v2-layout keeps its failure detail\". This head already changes that test's object writer, so BR-4 should start from this version of the test.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head a724b01c / tree 4e9f84b6. The builder lands. No deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:beb055ee3a42d918f0c5fd04157216a3066de3f0","binding":"assigned","head":"a724b01ca262dcb20b5f47c6c3b4d7a389c216bf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc2344b66c747921f28be89cf8991701ce4f05fb\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bde9081bba23acf3ca3ddf1d7accd8ddb11980f1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0087101872504c00efc4cf650c555b178be602d2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}